    "result_text": "All tests pass (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; the other files are support/base classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional owner `postcode` support with minimal structural impact by adding small, cohesive units rather than growing existing complex methods.\n\n**Changes (5 files):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema with `pattern: '^[0-9]{4}$'`. Since the generator has `performBeanValidation=true`, this produces a `@Pattern` on the generated DTO, so a malformed postcode (e.g. `\"12\"`) is rejected 400 automatically via `@Valid` \u2014 no Java validation code needed. `Owner` inherits the field via `allOf`, so both request and response DTOs gain it.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `postcode` column field plus a trivial getter/setter (CC=1 each). MapStruct auto-maps `postcode` by name in both directions, so `OwnerMapper` needed no changes.\n\n3. **`OwnerPostcodeAdvice.java`** (new) \u2014 A self-contained `RequestBodyAdvice` mirroring the existing `OwnerTelephoneLengthAdvice` pattern. It rejects (400) a 4-digit postcode that's out of range for the city's region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), while leaving unknown-region cities and absent postcodes untouched, and letting the `@Pattern` handle malformed values. Being a new small class, its surrounding complexity (WMC_other) is minimal.\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `postcode VARCHAR(4)` column (hsqldb is the complete, test-active schema; h2/postgres/mysql are already stale/incomplete, so I left them as-is per existing convention).\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 Added the extra `NULL` to the 10 seed rows' positional inserts.\n\n**Verification:** Full suite is green \u2014 `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The passing `coreStoresValidPostcode` confirms the store-and-return round-trip, `coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode` confirms backward-compatibility, and `errorRejectsMalformedPostcode` confirms 400 rejection.",
